WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:05.068
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.136 --> 00:08.472
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.539 --> 00:11.608
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.676 --> 00:14.578
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.646 --> 00:18.482
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.549 --> 00:21.418
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.486 --> 00:23.020
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.087 --> 00:24.388
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.455 --> 00:29.370
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.790 --> 00:38.537
Peter, I need you to
pick up the dry cleaning.

00:38.584 --> 00:39.418
Here's the ticket.

00:39.506 --> 00:40.907
It's the Chinese
one over on Elm.

00:40.974 --> 00:43.109
All right. Well, I need my
other white shirt back anyway.

00:43.177 --> 00:44.577
This one's getting
kind of smelly.

00:44.645 --> 00:45.945
And if I wore another color,

00:46.013 --> 00:47.346
I think it would
just throw people.

00:47.414 --> 00:48.815
You only have
two white shirts?

00:48.882 --> 00:50.817
Well, I had a third one,
but it got ruined

00:50.884 --> 00:52.785
at that wine tasting at
Michael J. Fox's house.

00:52.853 --> 00:54.654
Hi. I'm Peter Griffin.

00:54.722 --> 00:57.190
Now, we were going to show you
the actual scene,

00:57.257 --> 00:59.525
but it... it would just
make us all sad.

00:59.593 --> 01:02.328
So, I-I'm just going to
tell you what happened.

01:02.396 --> 01:05.298
See, he has this disease,
and it makes him shake a lot,

01:05.365 --> 01:06.933
and what with all the shaking,

01:07.000 --> 01:08.768
he spilled his wine
all over my shirt,

01:08.836 --> 01:10.703
and my shirt, uh, was ruined.

01:11.872 --> 01:13.573
So that's what that was.

01:13.640 --> 01:15.608
Um... I mean, he was
very nice about it.

01:15.676 --> 01:18.277
He said, he said,
"Send me the bill."

01:18.345 --> 01:21.881
<i>Which, I mean, that's not
how he said it, uh, but...</i>

01:21.949 --> 01:23.683
You know, we got there.

01:23.751 --> 01:26.085
Anyway, I sent him the bill,
and he sent me this check.

01:26.153 --> 01:28.554
But, uh... it's...

01:28.622 --> 01:29.989
I-I don't, I don't,
I don't think

01:30.057 --> 01:31.824
I'm going to be able
to cash this. Um...

01:31.892 --> 01:34.727
I don't... You'd think Tracy
Pollan would, would be in charge

01:34.795 --> 01:36.129
of the checkbook, you know?

01:36.196 --> 01:37.931
'Cause I mean, what else
is she doing right now?

01:37.999 --> 01:40.634
I don't, I don't think he's got
the leverage to Rita Wilson her

01:40.702 --> 01:42.836
around town anymore.
I mean, I-I, that's...

01:42.904 --> 01:44.238
I mean, that's
where it's gotten.

01:44.305 --> 01:46.840
So... Anyway, that's what
happened to my shirt.

01:46.908 --> 01:49.510
I'm glad we took the high road
on this one.

01:49.577 --> 01:50.978
Wh-what's that?

01:51.045 --> 01:53.413
Oh, wait, now they're telling me
they do want to show it.

01:53.481 --> 01:56.350
I really like the finish
on this Shiraz...

01:56.417 --> 01:58.819
Son of a bitch!
What is your problem?

02:03.124 --> 02:05.559
Aw, damn. Which one's
the Chinese one?

02:11.432 --> 02:12.833
That's probably it.

02:13.968 --> 02:16.136
(sensor makes "bing bong" sound)

02:16.204 --> 02:17.404
(bing bong)

02:17.472 --> 02:18.272
(bing bong)

02:18.339 --> 02:20.174
(bing bong)

02:21.910 --> 02:23.844
(bing bongs overlapping)

02:23.912 --> 02:26.079
You stop make bing bong!
Every bing bong two cent!

02:26.147 --> 02:27.247
What you want?

02:27.315 --> 02:29.883
Uh, yeah. I'm here to
pick up my cleaning?

02:31.119 --> 02:32.786
Aw, cool, look at that!

02:32.854 --> 02:35.055
Aw, this seems like it'd
be a great place to work.

02:35.123 --> 02:36.223
But I...

02:36.291 --> 02:39.527
I didn't go to college.

02:39.595 --> 02:40.662
That 20 dollar.

02:42.865 --> 02:44.566
Hey, uh, I think you
forgot my shirt.

02:44.633 --> 02:47.168
There no shirt.
Well, no, I know you
have my white shirt.

02:47.236 --> 02:48.670
Can you check again?
No need check.

02:48.737 --> 02:49.971
I no have your shirt.

02:50.039 --> 02:51.806
Listen here, Washee-Washee,
you do have my shirt.

02:51.874 --> 02:52.941
I no have your shirt.

02:53.008 --> 02:54.175
You yes have my shirt!

02:54.243 --> 02:55.743
You get out my store!
You get me shirt!

02:55.811 --> 02:57.879
You go or I call police!
You no dare call police!

02:57.947 --> 03:00.048
Oh, you want to play game,
fatso? You big, big...

03:00.115 --> 03:02.550
911!
Fine! I go.
But this no over.

03:02.618 --> 03:03.985
I take picture of Ang Lee.

03:04.053 --> 03:06.254
Good! He do too many white
people movie anyway!

03:06.322 --> 03:07.722
(bing bong)

03:07.790 --> 03:09.490
(bing bongs overlapping)

03:09.558 --> 03:11.426
You no come back, ever!

03:11.493 --> 03:14.596
I no like you American!
And all you American look alike!

03:14.663 --> 03:16.464
Oh, we all look alike, do we?

03:16.532 --> 03:18.833
Well, look who's talking!

03:22.304 --> 03:24.772
What do you mean we
can't go there anymore?

03:24.840 --> 03:26.641
Who gives a crap?
We'll get a new cleaners.

03:26.709 --> 03:29.110
They're all the same.
They are not
all the same!

03:29.178 --> 03:32.413
Peter, I have been going to
Mr. Washee-Washee for ten years,

03:32.481 --> 03:34.616
and I am not finding
another dry cleaner.

03:34.683 --> 03:36.751
Now we are going to
invite him over for dinner,

03:36.819 --> 03:38.620
and you are going
to apologize.

03:38.687 --> 03:40.555
(sighs)
All right, fine.

03:40.623 --> 03:41.723
MR. WASHEE-WASHEE:
Hello?

03:41.790 --> 03:44.326
Hi, Mr. Washee-Washee,
it's Peter Griffin.

03:44.394 --> 03:46.795
Um, my wife wants to invite
you over for dinner.

03:46.863 --> 03:48.931
What you having?
Number 32?

03:48.999 --> 03:49.832
Ooh!

03:54.204 --> 03:56.739
Peter, isn't there something
you'd like to say

03:56.806 --> 03:58.774
to Mr. Washee-Washee?

03:58.842 --> 03:59.942
(grumbles)

04:00.010 --> 04:01.143
Peter.

04:01.211 --> 04:02.711
Fine.

04:02.779 --> 04:05.481
Mr. Washee-Washee, I'm sorry
I was rude at your store.

04:05.548 --> 04:07.416
Is okay. I accept
your bad apology.

04:07.484 --> 04:08.884
Good. Now give me
back my shirt!

04:08.952 --> 04:10.452
Peter!
I no have your shirt!

04:10.520 --> 04:12.154
You yes have my shirt!
Enough!

04:12.222 --> 04:14.056
You all banned
from my store!

04:14.124 --> 04:15.057
Bing bong.

04:15.125 --> 04:17.092
Great, Peter.
Nice going.

04:17.160 --> 04:18.827
This dinner was
a disaster.

04:18.895 --> 04:20.996
<i>Eh, Clash of the Titans
owl was worse.</i>

04:21.064 --> 04:22.798
So you're from Greece.

04:22.866 --> 04:24.366
I've always wanted
to go there.

04:24.434 --> 04:25.401
What's it like?

04:25.468 --> 04:26.835
(whirring)

04:26.903 --> 04:28.437
(mechanical hooting)

04:28.505 --> 04:30.639
Yeah, I can't... I can't
understand a word he's saying.

04:30.707 --> 04:33.309
Yeah. I told you, Lois,
only Harry Hamlin can.

04:33.376 --> 04:34.743
If you're going to
invite the owl

04:34.811 --> 04:36.245
you got to invite
Harry Hamlin.

04:36.313 --> 04:39.248
I will not have Harry
Hamlin in this house.

04:42.452 --> 04:44.353
413, 413.

04:44.421 --> 04:46.056
I think this is it, Chris.

04:46.123 --> 04:48.959
<i>Ooh! The Mr. Sulu Show!</i>

04:49.026 --> 04:53.596
<i>(to Star Trek theme music)
♪ Sulu, he star of the show ♪</i>

04:55.599 --> 04:59.903
♪ Other guys just along
for the ride ♪

04:59.971 --> 05:02.839
He's got my shirt
in there, I can feel it.

05:02.907 --> 05:04.140
All right, I'm going inside.

05:15.553 --> 05:17.420
I knew it!

05:17.488 --> 05:19.089
Drop it, or I
blow you head off!

05:20.891 --> 05:22.392
Listen, Washee-Washee,
that's my shirt,

05:22.460 --> 05:23.727
and I ain't leaving
here without it.

05:23.794 --> 05:24.828
That no your shirt!

05:24.895 --> 05:25.729
Oh, yeah?

05:28.799 --> 05:30.066
Okay, it's not my shirt.

05:30.134 --> 05:33.136
You break in my house,
I can kill you legally.

05:33.204 --> 05:34.871
Fine, shoot me!
But you're going to
ruin the shirt.

05:34.939 --> 05:36.106
Take off shirt!

05:36.173 --> 05:38.274
Well, it seems we're
at an impasse.

05:38.342 --> 05:39.876
How do you propose
we settle this?

05:39.944 --> 05:42.712
We have fight.
But I pick venue.
Deal.

05:42.780 --> 05:44.614
(video game music plays)

05:46.283 --> 05:47.617
ANNOUNCER:
Round One.

05:47.685 --> 05:49.153
Fight!

05:49.221 --> 05:50.354
(shouts)

05:51.790 --> 05:53.958
(shouts)

05:54.026 --> 05:57.094
(shouting gibberish)

05:57.162 --> 05:59.096
(grunting)

06:04.202 --> 06:06.804
(cry echoes into distance)

06:08.006 --> 06:10.207
(cackling)

06:10.275 --> 06:11.809
You lose.

06:16.648 --> 06:18.549
Hi, I'm here
for Peter Griffin.

06:18.617 --> 06:19.650
Wait over there.

06:24.623 --> 06:27.191
Not the best way to spend
a Thursday night, huh?

06:27.259 --> 06:28.726
(sighs)
You can say that again.

06:28.794 --> 06:31.062
I was hoping to be at this
Democratic Party fundraiser.

06:31.129 --> 06:32.363
Oh, God, is that tonight?

06:32.431 --> 06:35.199
Aw... You know, I promised
Barry I'd be there.

06:35.267 --> 06:38.169
I, I call him "Barry," you
probably know him as "Barack."

06:38.236 --> 06:39.703
Um... yeah.

06:39.771 --> 06:41.439
So what are
you doing here?

06:41.506 --> 06:43.574
Ah, I'm picking up
my friend Peter.

06:43.642 --> 06:45.943
Are you picking up
a... boyfriend?

06:46.011 --> 06:50.414
No, actually. I got arrested for
protesting the Wal-Mart opening.

06:50.482 --> 06:52.384
Oh, yeah. I went to
the first part of that,

06:52.452 --> 06:53.718
but then some fireworks went off

06:53.786 --> 06:55.187
and I ran for two miles
straight.

06:55.254 --> 06:56.755
(laughs)

06:56.823 --> 06:58.590
I'm Denise.
I'm Brian.

06:58.658 --> 07:01.393
Hey, would you mind if
I asked for your number?

07:01.461 --> 07:03.562
Who knows? Maybe we could
get arrested together.

07:03.629 --> 07:04.696
(laughing)

07:04.764 --> 07:07.432
Sure. I'd like that.

07:07.500 --> 07:10.836
Number 3287.

07:10.903 --> 07:12.771
Come on, Peter.
I'm here to take you home.

07:12.839 --> 07:14.539
I don't know, Brian.

07:14.607 --> 07:17.042
This is the only world
I know anymore.

07:17.110 --> 07:18.877
Peter, you've been
in there for 15 minutes.

07:24.984 --> 07:26.818
Good morning,
everyone.

07:26.886 --> 07:28.720
Oh, crap,
he's in love again.

07:28.788 --> 07:30.789
I know, I know. But
this time it's for real.

07:30.857 --> 07:33.258
You know, I, I really feel
like Denise is the girl

07:33.326 --> 07:34.826
I've waited my whole life for.

07:34.894 --> 07:37.028
Oh, please, you've only
known her a week.

07:37.096 --> 07:38.663
Besides, I thought Jillian was

07:38.731 --> 07:40.265
the girl you waited
your whole life for.

07:40.333 --> 07:41.533
Well, Jillian was.

07:41.601 --> 07:43.168
But I'll, I'll never
get her back.

07:43.236 --> 07:45.604
But Denise... I really think
there's something special there.

07:45.671 --> 07:48.106
Brian, you went to one
protest rally with her.

07:48.174 --> 07:49.474
It's hardly a date.

07:49.542 --> 07:50.909
Oh yeah? You want to see?

07:50.977 --> 07:52.444
I'll call her right now
and ask her out to dinner.

07:55.315 --> 07:57.016
Hey, Denise?
It's me.

07:57.084 --> 07:59.285
Brian.

07:59.353 --> 08:00.386
Brian Griffin.

08:00.454 --> 08:01.854
STEWIE:
Oh, boy.

08:01.922 --> 08:04.157
Um, hey, listen, you know,
I've had such a great time

08:04.224 --> 08:06.125
hanging out with you,
and I was thinking...

08:06.193 --> 08:08.861
How about we go
on an actual date?

08:08.929 --> 08:10.296
Uh-huh.

08:10.364 --> 08:11.764
Sounds great!

08:11.832 --> 08:12.865
Bye.

08:12.933 --> 08:14.200
So?

08:14.268 --> 08:16.869
Well, guess who has
a date on Saturday?

08:16.937 --> 08:18.137
Not me.

08:18.205 --> 08:20.039
(sobbing)

08:21.608 --> 08:24.544
PETER:
Put the dog out.
The dog's crying.

08:24.611 --> 08:26.546
Can someone put... Lois!
Can someone put the dog out?

08:26.613 --> 08:27.647
I'm trying to read!

08:29.716 --> 08:32.084
(groans) What the hell?
What's the matter with you?

08:32.152 --> 08:33.753
Did an ambulance
go by or something?

08:47.558 --> 08:49.959
Hey, Brian... Aw, sweet!
Morning drinking!

08:51.695 --> 08:52.829
Whoo, yeah!

08:52.897 --> 08:54.230
Party!

08:54.298 --> 08:56.132
Peter, I'm not getting
drunk for fun.

08:56.200 --> 08:58.669
I'm, I'm drinking
because I'm sad.

08:58.737 --> 09:00.604
Because I'm never going to
meet the right woman.

09:00.672 --> 09:03.140
Because I'm... I'm going to
die old and alone.

09:03.208 --> 09:04.742
Oh, you're
Rip Torn drinking.

09:04.810 --> 09:06.310
Well, you know, listen.
Instead of sitting here

09:06.378 --> 09:07.812
feeling sorry for yourself,

09:07.879 --> 09:09.847
why don't you take Quagmire's
class on picking up chicks?

09:09.915 --> 09:11.148
Quagmire teaches a class?

09:11.216 --> 09:12.650
How come I've never
heard about this?

09:12.717 --> 09:14.919
'Cause Quagmire forbids us
to tell you about his life.

09:14.986 --> 09:16.720
As you may recall, he hates you.

09:16.788 --> 09:19.023
Ah, wouldn't help me anyway.
It's a hopeless situation.

09:19.090 --> 09:21.492
You know, if you ever want to
get anywhere with this girl,

09:21.560 --> 09:23.427
you gotta ditch that
negative attitude.

09:23.495 --> 09:25.129
You're, you're as
bad as Negatron.

09:25.197 --> 09:26.831
Do as I command,

09:26.898 --> 09:30.267
and we will defeat the Autobots
once and for all!

09:30.335 --> 09:31.602
Nope. Not going
to work.

09:31.670 --> 09:34.605
Oh, come on. What
did we talk about?

09:34.673 --> 09:36.040
Autobots always win.

09:36.107 --> 09:37.341
You think Optimus
Prime's gonna be dead,

09:37.409 --> 09:38.676
but then he's not dead.

09:38.743 --> 09:42.046
I'm taking this from a robot
that turns into a canoe?

09:42.113 --> 09:43.447
When there's a battle on

09:43.515 --> 09:45.115
a gently-moving river,
you'll want me.

09:50.055 --> 09:53.190
Now as I said before,
I can't make you into studs.

09:53.258 --> 09:56.193
I can only help you bring out
your "inner stud."

09:56.261 --> 09:57.695
But there's a lot
of potential here.

09:59.532 --> 10:00.999
Now how many of you guys think

10:01.067 --> 10:02.234
a woman is looking
for Prince Charming?

10:03.870 --> 10:05.770
Wrong! They're looking for
bastards like me!

10:05.838 --> 10:08.006
Well, I don't,
I don't know about that.

10:08.074 --> 10:10.976
Mort, How many times you been
laid since your wife died?

10:11.043 --> 10:12.544
Do Muriel's clothes count?

10:12.612 --> 10:14.079
No! You want to know

10:14.146 --> 10:16.681
how many times I've been laid
since last night? 60!

10:16.749 --> 10:19.718
Why? 'Cause I'm not trying
to be a girl's Prince Charming.

10:19.785 --> 10:21.152
I'm trying to be
that big mistake

10:21.220 --> 10:22.587
they made at the bar
last night.

10:22.655 --> 10:23.922
Look, what's the
first thing you say

10:23.990 --> 10:25.457
to a woman when you meet her?

10:25.525 --> 10:27.993
Pleased to meet you.
That's a handsome scarf pin.

10:28.060 --> 10:29.494
No! You say,

10:29.562 --> 10:31.830
"Hi, there. How's your
relationship with your father?"

10:31.898 --> 10:34.032
If she says anything
positive, move along.

10:34.100 --> 10:35.600
Hey. Sorry I'm late.

10:35.668 --> 10:37.636
Brian! What are
you doing here?

10:37.703 --> 10:39.337
I'm in your class.
What? No way!

10:39.405 --> 10:40.772
I don't want you in here!

10:40.840 --> 10:42.374
Too bad. Here's my
class receipt.

10:42.441 --> 10:43.708
Now teach me how
to find love.

10:43.776 --> 10:45.176
All right. Fine.

10:45.244 --> 10:47.812
But you lick yourself once in
this class and you're out!

10:50.182 --> 10:51.249
Don't look,
don't look!

10:51.317 --> 10:52.984
I spilled something.

10:53.052 --> 10:55.787
♪ ♪

11:00.526 --> 11:02.895
All right, time to practice
what we've learned.

11:02.963 --> 11:04.030
You're up, Brian.

11:04.097 --> 11:05.398
Now, go hit
on that fat chick.

11:05.465 --> 11:07.833
What? Why?
Do it or you get an "F".

11:07.901 --> 11:09.602
All right.

11:09.670 --> 11:11.571
Uh, excuse me.

11:11.638 --> 11:14.140
I was just looking you
over and I had a question.

11:14.207 --> 11:16.275
Are those highlights in
your hair or potato chips?

11:16.343 --> 11:17.877
Highlights!
Okay.

11:17.945 --> 11:20.880
Hey, will you sign this form
that says I hit on you?

11:20.948 --> 11:22.315
Sassy!

11:22.382 --> 11:25.518
You've got me sweating
above and below my ass.

11:25.586 --> 11:26.886
Let's go, lover.

11:31.458 --> 11:33.926
Okay, what the (bleep)?

11:33.994 --> 11:35.728
I know, I know.

11:35.796 --> 11:38.598
Quagmire told us to dress
flashy so girls would notice us.

11:38.665 --> 11:40.733
Oh, right, peacocking.
How's the class going?

11:40.801 --> 11:42.468
Well, so far so
good, I guess.

11:42.536 --> 11:43.769
But tonight's
the real test.

11:43.837 --> 11:45.705
I'm gonna try out what
I've learned on Denise.

11:45.772 --> 11:46.872
Well, good luck.

11:46.940 --> 11:48.107
Hey, who was that
fat chick

11:48.175 --> 11:49.475
sneaking out of
here this morning?

11:49.543 --> 11:52.445
Oh, that was someone
I met from class. Bettina.

11:52.512 --> 11:54.714
Ooh, that's way too
fancy a name for her.

11:54.781 --> 11:56.949
Her name should be
"Thud" or-- or "Oof."

11:59.019 --> 12:02.822
♪ ♪

12:02.889 --> 12:06.193
You know, I have to admit,
Brian, I'm glad you called.

12:06.260 --> 12:07.561
I sort of missed
hanging out.

12:07.629 --> 12:08.762
Call me The Paw.

12:08.830 --> 12:10.464
That's what I go
by now, The Paw.

12:10.531 --> 12:11.965
Oh, okay.

12:12.033 --> 12:13.066
Yeah.

12:13.134 --> 12:14.968
A lot of babes
here tonight.

12:15.036 --> 12:17.738
Shut up for a couple minutes,
I'm gonna look around.

12:17.805 --> 12:19.539
Uh, Brian, you're being
kind of disrespectful.

12:19.607 --> 12:20.841
Ah, relax, baby.

12:20.908 --> 12:22.843
Hey, check your phone.
I sent you something.

12:22.910 --> 12:25.345
(gasps) Oh, my God!
Is-- is that your...?

12:25.413 --> 12:28.248
Yeah. How'd you like to get hit
in the face with that?

12:28.316 --> 12:29.549
Okay, you know what?
I'm gonna go.

12:29.617 --> 12:31.084
Why, you getting
more moles put on?

12:31.152 --> 12:33.553
You know, I came here 'cause
I thought I'd made a mistake

12:33.621 --> 12:35.122
by not giving you a chance,

12:35.189 --> 12:38.125
but it's obvious you're
just another typical jerk.

12:38.192 --> 12:40.727
Denise, wait...

12:43.631 --> 12:45.599
All right, let's see
what you guys have done

12:45.667 --> 12:46.867
to make yourselves look
like douchebags.

12:46.934 --> 12:48.268
You're a son of a bitch.

12:48.336 --> 12:50.804
You're teaching us all this
crap about how to get women

12:50.872 --> 12:52.539
and it's all a
bunch of bull!

12:52.607 --> 12:55.275
I came here 'cause
I wanted to get Denise back

12:55.343 --> 12:57.210
and instead, you
ruined my life!

12:57.278 --> 12:59.913
These skills aren't for women
you care about, you idiot.

12:59.981 --> 13:02.149
This course is in getting
laid, not finding love.

13:02.216 --> 13:03.583
So, what's the point?

13:03.651 --> 13:06.653
If you never find love, then
it's just meaningless sex.

13:06.721 --> 13:08.656
How will I get the woman
of my dreams?

13:08.724 --> 13:10.058
Only when you're ready.

13:10.125 --> 13:11.993
And maybe not even then.

13:12.061 --> 13:15.029
<i>You see, women are a lot like
Saturday Night Live sketches.</i>

13:15.097 --> 13:16.597
Lots of them are awful,
some are decent,

13:16.665 --> 13:18.566
and a few are pretty good.

13:18.634 --> 13:21.469
But then there's that one--
that one woman

13:21.537 --> 13:24.772
who's as amazingly perfect
as "Massive Head Wound Harry."

13:24.840 --> 13:28.176
For me, that woman
is Cheryl Tiegs.

13:28.243 --> 13:29.844
You'd never fall
for these tricks.

13:29.912 --> 13:31.879
That's why I keep trying
to figure out

13:31.947 --> 13:33.681
how to bring you
back into my life.

13:33.749 --> 13:35.316
So we can make it work.

13:35.384 --> 13:37.585
I still remember the day we met.

13:39.955 --> 13:41.856
Hey-ho, look at the man
on the unicycle.

13:41.924 --> 13:44.092
Look at the man on the unicycle
with a parrot on his shoulder.

13:44.159 --> 13:46.094
Hey-ho, put five cents
in the hat.

13:46.161 --> 13:47.762
That's quite a skill
you've got the.

13:47.830 --> 13:49.964
Well, ever since I got
discharged from the Navy,

13:50.032 --> 13:51.733
I do anything I can
to make money.

13:51.800 --> 13:53.835
I'm thinking about getting
my pilot's license.

13:53.902 --> 13:56.070
Well, I think
unicycles are sexy.

13:59.174 --> 14:02.143
Glenn, these past few weeks
have been amazing.

14:02.211 --> 14:04.278
I think I'm falling
in love with you.

14:04.346 --> 14:06.314
I know. I feel the same way.

14:06.381 --> 14:07.882
If this is the kind of joy

14:07.950 --> 14:10.284
the '80s has in store
for me, I'm ready.

14:10.352 --> 14:13.489
<i>But that wasn't the case.</i>

14:13.556 --> 14:16.091
<i>In fact, things went
wrong real fast.</i>

14:16.159 --> 14:17.926
♪ ♪

14:21.598 --> 14:24.533
Uh, Cheryl, don't you think
it's time for us to go now?

14:24.601 --> 14:25.934
Why? We just got here?

14:26.002 --> 14:27.102
I'm having a good time.

14:27.170 --> 14:28.470
Yeah, I can tell.

14:28.538 --> 14:30.739
You've been talking to
John Davidson for half an hour.

14:30.807 --> 14:32.541
Hey, Glenn, great
to meet you.

14:32.609 --> 14:34.309
<i>John Davidson, host
of That's Incredible.</i>

14:34.377 --> 14:36.111
Oh, hey, John.
I like your work...

14:36.179 --> 14:37.646
not!

14:37.714 --> 14:39.515
<i>That was the first time
anybody ever used that.</i>

14:39.582 --> 14:40.949
<i>First time, I swear to God.</i>

14:41.017 --> 14:43.952
Glenn, I've about had it
with your petty jealousy.

14:44.020 --> 14:46.188
I'm starting to think this
relationship is a mistake.

14:46.256 --> 14:48.724
Well, maybe it is.

14:48.792 --> 14:51.693
Wow, did you just break up
with Cheryl Tiegs?

14:51.761 --> 14:53.262
I sure did.

14:53.329 --> 14:54.797
What do you think
of that, folks?

14:54.864 --> 14:57.166
ALL:
That's incredible!

15:01.237 --> 15:04.673
Someday...
someday we'll make it right.

15:04.741 --> 15:07.309
You shouldn't have tried
these tricks on Denise, Brian.

15:07.377 --> 15:09.144
But if you ask me,
she got lucky,

15:09.212 --> 15:10.879
because now she's dodged
the bullet of being

15:10.947 --> 15:12.681
in a relationship with
a loser like you.

15:12.749 --> 15:14.784
Well, you just think you know
everything, don't you?

15:14.852 --> 15:16.986
Y-You're like a black
woman in hindsight.

15:17.054 --> 15:19.222
I told you.
What did I tell you?

15:19.290 --> 15:21.658
Didn't I tell you?
'Cause I told you.

15:21.725 --> 15:24.027
Mm-hmm, and when
did I tell you?

15:24.094 --> 15:25.395
A long time ago.

15:25.462 --> 15:27.997
And what did I say would
happen when I told you?

15:28.065 --> 15:30.099
Exactly what just happened.

15:34.138 --> 15:35.839
(doorbell ringing)

15:39.543 --> 15:42.178
Wha... Are... Are you...

15:42.246 --> 15:43.379
Cheryl?!

15:43.447 --> 15:44.614
Hi, Glenn.

15:44.682 --> 15:46.549
Oh, my God. Cheryl.

15:46.617 --> 15:48.017
Wha-- what are
you doing here?

15:48.085 --> 15:49.619
Well, you know, it's
been so many years,

15:49.687 --> 15:50.920
and I was in the neighborhood,

15:50.988 --> 15:52.989
and I thought I'd just
drop by and say hi.

15:53.057 --> 15:55.592
My new boyfriend I guess knows
you, and told me where you live.

15:55.659 --> 15:57.160
(car horn honks)

15:57.228 --> 16:00.096
Hey, Cheryl, get your fat ass
over here before I dump you.

16:00.164 --> 16:02.098
He's so bossy.

16:02.166 --> 16:03.299
I love it.

16:03.367 --> 16:05.335
Well, it was great
seeing you, Glenn.

16:13.644 --> 16:15.378
(laughing)

16:23.765 --> 16:25.132
(loud pounding)

16:25.205 --> 16:26.372
QUAGMIRE:
Where is he?!

16:26.440 --> 16:28.841
Where's that
son of a bitch?!

16:28.909 --> 16:30.743
Whoa, whoa.
What's going on, Quagmire?

16:30.811 --> 16:32.344
You dirty bastard.

16:32.412 --> 16:33.946
I always knew
you were low,

16:34.014 --> 16:37.216
but you're nothing more than
a back-stabbing, junkyard cur.

16:37.284 --> 16:39.351
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
what the hell, man?

16:39.419 --> 16:42.388
My whole life's been
dedicated to Cheryl Tiegs!

16:42.456 --> 16:43.756
Yeah, I know. So what?

16:43.824 --> 16:45.291
Your dog is dating her!

16:45.358 --> 16:46.358
No way.

16:46.426 --> 16:48.027
You're banging Cheryl Tiegs?

16:48.094 --> 16:50.196
Yeah.
Oh, my God.

16:50.263 --> 16:51.564
Light the beacons.

16:51.631 --> 16:53.265
(fanfare playing)

17:03.577 --> 17:05.344
♪ ♪

17:23.631 --> 17:26.199
♪ ♪

17:35.142 --> 17:37.043
Cheryl Tiegs.

17:37.111 --> 17:38.245
Nice.

17:40.748 --> 17:44.651
♪ ♪

17:44.719 --> 17:48.855
I really like
this restaurant.

17:48.923 --> 17:50.657
Brian, you're acting
a little distant.

17:50.725 --> 17:51.958
Yeah, get whatever you want.

17:52.026 --> 17:55.395
Oh, hey guys, fancy me
running into you here.

17:55.463 --> 17:57.130
Oh, hey, Quagmire.

17:57.198 --> 17:59.266
Listen, Brian, I--
I've been a real heel,

17:59.333 --> 18:01.501
and I'd like
to make it up to you.

18:01.569 --> 18:05.372
Oh, well, that's very kind of
you, but there-there's no need.

18:05.439 --> 18:07.674
No, no, no, no,
I-I-I-I want to. I want to.

18:07.742 --> 18:09.809
In fact, you know, since
you guys are already here,

18:09.877 --> 18:12.045
I'd like to treat
the four of us to dinner.

18:12.113 --> 18:14.381
Well, sure, I...
wait, who's the fourth?

18:14.448 --> 18:15.882
Oh, my new girlfriend.

18:15.950 --> 18:17.117
Here she is.

18:17.184 --> 18:18.218
Jillian?

18:18.286 --> 18:19.619
Hi, Brian.

18:19.687 --> 18:20.820
How are you?

18:20.888 --> 18:22.123
Oh, he's doing great.

18:22.190 --> 18:23.624
Isn't that
right, pal?

18:23.692 --> 18:26.394
Guy looks like a million bucks,
all green and wrinkly, right?

18:26.461 --> 18:27.828
Oh, get in here.

18:27.896 --> 18:29.931
Ha-ha, hey, ho, ho,
whoa, heh.

18:29.998 --> 18:32.833
Okay, let's, uh,
let's have dinner, huh?

18:35.170 --> 18:38.205
So, uh, how did you
guys get together?

18:38.273 --> 18:40.641
Um, he showed up at my door

18:40.709 --> 18:42.710
and said he was
a Federal Boob Inspector.

18:42.778 --> 18:46.480
And I was gonna tell him to
go away, but he had a warrant.

18:46.548 --> 18:48.015
It was a Snickers
wrapper, Brian.

18:48.083 --> 18:49.550
I held up a
Snickers wrapper.

18:49.618 --> 18:51.852
But then he started saying
things to me

18:51.920 --> 18:54.388
that my father might say
if he were still alive,

18:54.456 --> 18:57.191
and I knew I liked him.

18:57.259 --> 18:59.060
Well, I guess you guys have
gotten pretty close, huh?

18:59.127 --> 19:01.696
Did Quagmire ever tell you
he was obese as a child?

19:01.763 --> 19:03.598
Did Brian ever tell you
he once had a tick

19:03.665 --> 19:06.167
on the back of his neck that he
couldn't reach with his mouth,

19:06.234 --> 19:08.369
and it swelled up to the
size of a ping-pong ball?

19:08.437 --> 19:09.937
Well, it was still smaller
than that thing

19:10.005 --> 19:11.439
you had on your lip
for three years.

19:11.506 --> 19:13.107
Oh, three years?
You mean like

19:13.175 --> 19:15.042
the three years you
have left on this planet?

19:15.110 --> 19:16.444
Oh, that's nice.

19:16.511 --> 19:18.813
Hey, if you guys are so
close, maybe Jillian should know

19:18.880 --> 19:20.681
that you teach a class
in picking up women.

19:20.749 --> 19:22.817
And Cheryl should know
that you took that class.

19:22.884 --> 19:25.053
Does Jillian know you're half
Polish, Mr. Quagglechek?

19:25.121 --> 19:26.254
You son of a bitch!

19:27.924 --> 19:29.358
(snarling)

19:32.462 --> 19:34.830
Enough. Stop it,
both of you.

19:34.897 --> 19:37.132
You obviously have
no respect for either of us.

19:37.200 --> 19:39.334
Yeah, you're
acting all mean.

19:39.402 --> 19:42.604
Now I'm glad you made me
face away during sex.

19:42.672 --> 19:45.140
Maybe you boys will get
it together someday,

19:45.208 --> 19:47.376
but it looks like that's
all you are-- boys.

19:47.443 --> 19:48.877
Yeah. Boys.

19:48.945 --> 19:50.779
Yay, I helped.

19:50.847 --> 19:52.714
Cheryl, wait.
Jillian.

19:52.782 --> 19:54.716
I'm sorry.
I'll do anything, please.

19:59.122 --> 20:00.522
Meg?

20:00.590 --> 20:02.758
Yeah, this still
happens sometimes.

20:08.231 --> 20:09.831
Hey.

20:09.899 --> 20:11.033
You okay?

20:11.100 --> 20:12.100
Yep.

20:12.168 --> 20:13.602
Just waiting for my car.

20:15.672 --> 20:19.274
Look, I'm sorry
I did what I did.

20:19.342 --> 20:22.678
Cheryl's great,
and I hope someday

20:22.745 --> 20:24.312
you get the chance
to be with her.

20:24.380 --> 20:27.082
No. I'm never gonna get
that chance again.

20:27.150 --> 20:29.185
I blew it for good, Brian.

20:29.253 --> 20:30.553
And you know what?

20:30.621 --> 20:32.021
I deserve to be lonely.

20:32.089 --> 20:33.423
I'm no saint.

20:33.490 --> 20:35.591
I dated Jillian
just to hurt you.

20:35.659 --> 20:37.193
It's okay.

20:37.261 --> 20:39.862
It probably wouldn't have worked
out, like everything else.

20:39.930 --> 20:42.265
Hey, you know,
may-maybe it took us

20:42.332 --> 20:44.500
stealing each other's girls
to finally become friends.

20:44.568 --> 20:45.735
Yeah, maybe.

20:51.709 --> 20:54.377
Oh, hey, uh, listen,
Cheryl actually drove me,

20:54.445 --> 20:56.713
and I spent all my cash
in the restaurant

20:56.780 --> 20:59.148
even... even... even though
you said you'd pay.

20:59.216 --> 21:01.784
So, uh, would you mind
giving me a lift home, buddy?

21:01.785 --> 22:02.785
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru